Artificial ORCA-4.2.1-style output for absspectra examples.

Not a real calculation. One strong sharp band at 25000 cm-1 (400 nm) plus a
cluster of eight weak transitions spread from 16000 to 19000 cm-1. Broadened,
the cluster sums to a low, wide, isolated hump near 17500 cm-1 (~571 nm) whose
prominence is well below the peak threshold. Plain --peaks reports only the
400 nm band; --peaks-force additionally marks the hump as a WAVE.

                * O   R   C   A *

